 Spatial averaging across the Dublin domain may smooth localized high-intensity rainfall, the 6-hour subsampling omits the intervening hourly evolution and limits the representation of rapidly evolving events, and upper-tail precipitation remains relatively sparse in the dataset. The controlled Bernoulli--Gamma comparison improved overall probabilistic scores but retained upper-tail undercoverage. Future work should assess higher-resolution observations and the transferability of the tested training and distribution choices to other settings, with joint evaluation of overall accuracy, event detection and false alarms. Evaluation across additional regions would also help determine how well the observed model behaviour generalizes beyond the Dublin setting.
 
